[h1]Phobos Manufacturing[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.1.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - unpublished draft

Refining and chemistry aboard your ship: turn what the crew mines into water, metal stock and oxygen, and keep the hydrogen. Realistic chemistry within the game's units, with the game's own dangers when it goes wrong.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Fennmark V4 Volatiles Refinery (4 x 4, 24 kW): bake hydrates or the new clay hydrates chunk for water, roast carbon ore for carbon stock (it breathes CO2, CO and smoke into the room: run a scrubber), cast meteoric iron into nickel-iron ingots, and with Shipbreaker melt four ingots with one carbon into its steel ingots. Water goes to a linked S3 or R3 vessel within one tile.
[*]Fennmark X2 Chemical Processor (2 x 2, 6 kW): water electrolysis. Every hour 1.125 kg of water becomes 1.000 kg of oxygen, into a linked O2 canister or the cabin air, and 0.125 kg of hydrogen into a linked H2 store.
[*]Fennmark H2 Hydrogen Store (2 x 2): 24 kg of hydrogen with a vent overboard. Damaged, it leaks to space; with oxygen and a spark, fire or hot hearth nearby, it burns through the game's own explosion.
[*]Clay hydrates now turn up in dark-regolith rock and C-class deposits. Ores are mined, never bought; nothing new is sold in shops.
[*]Version 0.1.0 is the first operational release: the three machines, five materials, a local Control Panel, C1 listing with Shipbreaker, and the same merchant and salvage routes as the sibling mods.
[/list]

[h2]Operating limits[/h2]
The V4 and X2 pause after a reload until you press Start. A melt left waiting for a cool room longer than its own run freezes into slag. Water needs a Shipbreaker S3 or Agriculture R3 within one tile. The steel charge needs Shipbreaker 0.38.0 or newer. No crew loading orders, no construction recipes (buy the machines), no Sabatier stage yet. Offline checks are not gameplay validation; in-game review is pending.

[h2]Requirements and installation[/h2]
Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.41.0 or newer. Shipbreaker 0.38.0 or newer and Agriculture are optional.

This is an unpublished development package. Automated checks do not establish in-game readiness or Unity layout approval. Keep required mods installed for saves using their content. Updating does not refill shops or old loot containers. See the installation guide for current download availability.

[h2]English wording update[/h2]
Controls, warnings and descriptions use clearer language. Equipment identities, saved progress, recipes and gameplay values are unchanged.

[h2]Guides, sources and credits[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games, Kitfox Games or the research institutions cited in the guides. Research informs design; compact equipment, yields and operating limits remain gameplay choices.
Original artwork uses AI-assisted production; artwork provenance and licensing are recorded separately.

